0,Benue–Congo languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benue–Congo_languages,"Benue–Congo is a major branch of the Volta-Congo languages which covers most of Sub-Saharan Africa.The neighbouring Volta–Niger branch of Nigeria and Benin is sometimes called ""West Benue–Congo"", but it does not form a united branch with Benue–Congo.",Bassa-Kontagora,Niger-Congo
1,Bassa-Kontagora jezik – Wikipedija,https://hr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bassa-Kontagora_jezik,"Bassa-Kontagora jezik (ISO 639-3: bsr), gotocvo izumrli nigersko-kongoanski jezik iz Nigerije, kojim je govorilo svega 10 ljudi (1987) od 30 000 etničkih Bassa u nigerijskoj državi Niger, LGA Mariga.",Bassa-Kontagora,Niger-Congo
2,Bassa-Kontagora Language (BSR)... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/bsr/,Bassa-Kontagora is a dormant language of Nigeria. It belongs to the Niger-Congo language family. The language is no longer used as a first language by any remaining members of the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.,Bassa-Kontagora,Niger-Congo
3,Basa-Kontagora language,https://grokipedia.com/page/basa_kontagora_language,"Basa-Kontagora, also known as Bassa-Kontagora, is an extinct Kainji language of the Niger-Congo family, formerly spoken in Niger State, Nigeria, particularly around Mariga and Kontagora.",Bassa-Kontagora,Niger-Congo
4,Endangered Languages Project - Bassa-Kontagora,https://www.endangeredlanguages.com/lang/3807,"Also known as. Basa, Basa-Kontagora. CLASSIFICATION. Niger-Congo, Atlantic-Congo, Benue-Congo, Kainji. Code authority. Iso 639-3.",Bassa-Kontagora,Niger-Congo
5,Bassa-Kontagora,https://docs.verbix.com/EndangeredLanguages/BassaKontagora,"Language: Bassa-Kontagora. Alternate names: Basa, Basa-Kontagora. Language code: bsr. Language family: Niger-Congo, Atlantic-Congo, Volta-Congo, Benue-Congo, Kainji, Western, Basa (SIL classification). Number of speakers: 10.",Bassa-Kontagora,Niger-Congo
